ght":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A metallic hollow waveguide has a cut-off frequency of 2 GHz for its dominant mode of operation.<br />\nIf the guide dimensions for its cross-section are in the ratio 1 : 2, the first degenerate TE and TM modes have a cutoff frequency of _____ GHz.</p>\n<p>(upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4.472","high":"4.472"},"solution":"<p>4.472 (4.20 - 4.80)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/d062db5cdf31fd7b76904ee3da3776303e990a8f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The volume charge density on a material is known to vary with time obeying the differential equation</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/2e6eee8cce6bc976130d67a5b415630f40e3bebd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/7c9518cfa8a8cac39479015ce4bf4e28ac2c1369.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/b3eecb2b115455d25d22f5626dbffe0269f336f2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/06df203d8b6a1cf56d1389426b0f1575d16f2a00.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/7fbac1839b665836923e936d10a1d1fceecb6478.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the below statements are correct regarding electromagnetic theory?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Electric field intensity at any point is the negative of the potential gradient at that point.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Electric field due to a finite line charge at a point is independent of the length of the line charge.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","t