6a91a5360cfad33c5ca14fd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":26,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The power radiated from the half wave dipole at 2 km away with magnetic field at point <img src=\"/media/39d49864198d8669db9e5fcce305f0002c62b7bf.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" />  as 10 μ A/m is _________ Watts. (upto three decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.576","high":"0.576"},"solution":"<p>0.576 (0.450 - 0.650)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/385824a7029170daf488848283809bc8c66f295f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":27,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n A non-magnetic good conductor supports a uniform plane wave travelling with a velocity of 1.8 × 10<sup>6</sup> m/s. If the wavelength <img src=\"/media/0d1734648af1a7f3d19afd41b9a9c5906d8b636e.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> = 0.28 mm, then the conductivity of this non-magnetic medium is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/eaa7e8c2ebcb8730562d1576441a83403ef0a3ed.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/c3a03c1d78d6334c3fc9341163d42dc7dc97c362.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/8ba06e76a3a4fdaa50d54df529c482b7d8eeb0a2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/b57a36e1371dce9e962883e753b49c70388efd94.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/ae1587955f183ec2f38be740095cba3e945bb16b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":28,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In a lossless non-magnetic medium, the peak value of electric field is given as 12 V/m . If the relative permittivity is given as <img src=\"/media/b4f5b499e2ac5e53c450840cbb69c1e8cc3378d9.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> then the time averaged power (in W/m<sup>2</sup>) will be _________. (upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.61","high":"0.61"},"solution":"<p>0.61 (0.58 - 0.64)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/3bfb9e12697fabc7b657dd3b8d99df16ea01655d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":29,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n It is required to propagate 30 GHz signal in an air-filled rectangular waveguide in TE<sub>01</sub> mode in such a way that <img src=\"/media/81f26cb995ac4881acd7e7ae14d77718bf1ba83b.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> If the dimensions of the waveguide are</p>\n<p>\n (<em>a</em> × <em>b</em>) and <em>a</em> > <em>b</em>, then the narrow wall dimension of the waveguide is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 0.83 cm</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0.36 cm</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1.2 cm</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 2.4 cm</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c4059bb5f51d6bc1d90cb2671ebd004d24bad423.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":30,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following condition is true for boundary conditions between conductor and a perfect dielectric?<br />\n (Assume the interface has charge density ρ<sub>s</sub>)</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/a2abf30863d028ad19ede61595ac867a50e3f995.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/55a24a0705759537f9266d06cde3653ac2f4a525.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/1c4293860766c65705e8773e78d6ac609910f5b8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/b47c8519f76197c66741730563f14342554bc2d1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a, b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d659d3775cbe3b106a660d01327da675ade99970.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":31,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n A uniform plane wave in air is normally incident on a dielectric material (σ = 0, μ<em><sub>r</sub></em> = 1, ∈<em><sub>r</sub></em> = 3). The electric field of the transmitted wave is given by <img src=\"/media/9723136b17251267e2d61f447938ee3b6c21292d.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> The electric field expression of the incident wave is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/0beac3d40622354ad84770b33875fdd4168a3811.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/a2af894d779214974feb7d5492a5aced4c72b2b2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/a78ef103c6f10517d6bb8a58e5def6ff7d00d6a4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/0234cef896d27a26e0cd53c4be151d460e1d9c6f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/df56eb7a64759806ecf45bd41f60537d4ae50230.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":32,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In a non-magnetic medium,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/6e5b7aebb64409ead10dff39cb07ede1f5b0ba61.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The intrinsic impedance of the medium is ________ Ω. (upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"112.79","high":"112.79"},"solution":"<p>112.79 (112.50 - 113.00)</p>\